alter table engagement_preferences
  add column off_ramp_sent_at timestamptz,
  add column earned_third_send boolean not null default false,
  add column is_control_group boolean;

comment on column engagement_preferences.off_ramp_sent_at is 'Story P2-1 (pre-emptive off-ramp) — stamped when the off-ramp offer (fewer texts / different food / stop entirely) fires for the account''s CURRENT non-engagement streak, so it fires once per streak rather than once per qualifying send. Nulled by lib/cadenceDecay.js#recordEngagedSend whenever the streak resets (any engaged reply), so a later streak can trigger the offer again. See lib/offRamp.js for the fire/no-fire decision and off_ramp_events for the distinct event log (an offer, not an automatic reduction — see that table''s comment for why it is logged separately from cadence-decay events).';
comment on column engagement_preferences.earned_third_send is 'Story P2-3 — a rolling, continuously re-evaluated (not permanent) eligibility flag for a 3rd weekly send, earned when the account engaged with at least 1 of its last 3 scheduled status=sent engagement_sends rows (see lib/thirdSendEligibility.js). Deliberately a separate column from cadence_tier (which per A11 only ever decays) so earning and decaying never collide on the same field — an account can be earned_third_send=true and still get only 2 sends/week if cadence_tier has decayed off standard (see engagementScheduler.js#effectiveSendCount, which requires BOTH). Control-group accounts (is_control_group) never earn this — see lib/thirdSendEligibility.js.';
comment on column engagement_preferences.is_control_group is 'Story P2-5 — 10% control group, assigned once via a deterministic hash of account_id (lib/controlGroup.js#isControlGroupAccount) the first time the account becomes send-eligible (profile.isReady, see engagementSuppression.js#checkSuppression). NULL means not yet assigned (the account has never crossed MIN_UPLOADS_FOR_PROFILE) — treated identically to false everywhere is_control_group is read, so nullability is safe. Because the hash is a pure function of account_id (not a live random roll), re-evaluating it is always idempotent — "assigned once" is a write-optimization, not a correctness requirement. Control-group accounts get fixed generic (deal-strength-only) scoring instead of profile-weighted scoring (lib/engagementScoring.js#scoreCandidatesControlGroup), stay on the fixed default send-day/send-count schedule (excluded from P2-2''s personalization and P2-3''s earned 3rd send), but otherwise go through suppression, slot policy, repetition guard, and templates identically to a treatment account — and hard/soft opt-out machinery is completely unaffected by this flag.';
